<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Chōkei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1343–1394</span> · <a href="/centuries/14th-century">14th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Chōkei (1343–1394) was the third emperor of the Southern Court of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a>, reigning from 1368 to 1383 after his father Go-Murakami. A firm opponent of compromise with the Ashikaga <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shogun">shogunate</a>, he was officially recognised as a legitimate emperor only in 1926, after historians established that he had reigned. He abdicated in favour of his brother Go-Kameyama.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/emperor-chokei.jpg" alt="Emperor Chōkei" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 明治天皇聖徳奉讃会 · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emperor_Chokei.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
